## Proof Interpretation
The bad core exists in many local cells, but every audited row leaves at least one survivor.
Every local core interval is covered by small odd-owner sets in each branch; the global task is to show these local covers cannot concatenate across all E_safe components.
This is a sharper target than a scalar union bound: HYP-3434's overlap tax is the branch-one-dimensional shadow of the same owner-cover compression.
Endpoint labels show what the quotient is allowed to forget: raw order and endpoint openness may be forgotten, but branch color, owner speed, and E-safe component address may not.

## Tournament Analysis
vertices=proof obligations/certificate interfaces; alternate vertex sets considered: safe components, bad-core intervals, endpoint events, odd-owner cover tokens, Fourier modes, and runners
chosen_vertex_set=proof obligations plus interval-cover certificate interfaces
pairwise_observable=exactness + predicate retention + endpoint-owner recoverability + two-adic induction payload + scalar-firewall compliance
switch=higher weighted proof-facing score; ties by declared code order
tie_hamiltonian_path=B00_minimal_bad_core_cover_extractor -> B01_two_color_failure_normal_form -> B02_endpoint_owner_set_cover_lemma -> B03_overlap_tax_discharge_bridge -> B04_component_spine_router -> B05_two_adic_descent_induction -> B06_owner_current_exception_exit -> B07_harmonic_scalar_sidecar -> B08_raw_topology_or_named_constant
score_hist={-1: 1, 45: 1, 97: 1, 102: 1, 106: 1, 109: 1, 116: 1, 122: 1, 130: 1}
directed_3cycles=0
edge_flips_against_scalar_first=36
quotient_preserves=exact E_safe minus B0_odd cap B1_odd survivor predicate
quotient_destroys=open endpoint convention and raw runner ordering only
challenged_assumption=tournament vertices need not be runners/arcs; the useful tournament is over proof obligations and cover certificates

## Candidate Lemma
For every primitive covering row S=O union 2E with |S|=13, the local minimal covers of
E_safe cap B0_odd cap B1_odd cannot form a connected all-component cover unless an
owner-current exception, endpoint-spine failure, or two-adic descent debt is emitted.
A proof can now aim at a finite labelled packet theorem over minimal branch-owner covers
instead of attempting to prove a uniform positive branch-measure lower bound first.
